WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.800
Naming a single chicken and describing its habits reduces how often preschoolers select poultry for their meals. This is Planetterrian Daily, Episode 216. Researchers at SWPS University tested five and six-year-old children in two experiments that varied how an animal was presented, with the work appearing in the journal appetite. In the first experiment, one group received a silhouette of a chicken named Lelek, along with details on its favorite foods and yard habits. While the control group received only a general species

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:35.340
description. Children who heard the individual details built toy sandwiches with fewer poultry

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.240
slices than those who heard the general account. The reduction occurred only among children

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:45.240
who already showed low or moderate interest in meat. In the second experiment, presenting

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.260
the chicken as a unique individual produced stronger reluctance to eat poultry than presenting it as

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:55.800
one of many similar birds. The effect remained limited to the same species and left choices about

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:01.954
pork unchanged. Wild you hadras snails in a Japanese mountain valley coiled their shells in both

00:01:01.954 --> 00:01:07.934
directions, and individuals of opposite coil can still mate. University of Nottingham and

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:13.154
Tahoku University researchers report in current biology that sequence differences in the

00:01:13.154 --> 00:01:18.894
milestone gene change how cells twist during the earliest embryonic stages. Both left coiling

00:01:18.894 --> 00:01:23.794
and right coiling forms develop into healthy adults without disease or developmental defects.

00:01:23.794 --> 00:01:30.434
The less common left coiling variant shows molecular signatures of natural selection across evolutionary time.

00:01:31.034 --> 00:01:35.794
The same milestone protein participates in building the cell scaffold used by many animals.

00:01:36.742 --> 00:01:41.442
Most people assume a body's left-right layout is locked in from the first days of an embryo,

00:01:41.762 --> 00:01:43.702
and that flipping it always means disease.

00:01:44.322 --> 00:01:49.762
In these snails, the coiling direction is set by small sequence differences in the gene that codes from milestone.

00:01:49.762 --> 00:01:54.602
a protein that helps cells move and reshape themselves by interacting with the internal

00:01:54.602 --> 00:01:55.502
cell scaffold.

00:01:56.122 --> 00:02:00.302
During the first cell divisions, those sequence variants change whether cells twist clockwise

00:02:00.302 --> 00:02:01.602
or counter-clockwise.

00:02:02.162 --> 00:02:06.842
That initial twist then propagates through the embryo and sets not only the final coiling

00:02:06.842 --> 00:02:09.962
of the shell, but also the placement of internal organs.

00:02:10.542 --> 00:02:13.962
Both coiling forms have existed for a long evolutionary time.

00:02:14.622 --> 00:02:18.722
The valley population lets left coiling and right coiling snails exchange genes.

00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:24.222
A natural experiment that avoids the reproductive isolation opposite coiling usually causes.

00:02:24.802 --> 00:02:29.902
A different gene mutation in pond snails produces left coiling animals that also show developmental

00:02:29.902 --> 00:02:30.882
abnormalities.

00:02:31.362 --> 00:02:34.602
So not every change in chirality genes is equally benign.

00:02:35.182 --> 00:02:40.142
The same myosin-based cell scaffold machinery operates in many animals, including humans,

00:02:40.522 --> 00:02:43.542
where organ reversals are rare and often linked to health issues.

00:02:43.542 --> 00:02:48.982
What remains unclear is exactly which additional molecular steps convert that early cell twist

00:02:48.982 --> 00:02:53.922
difference into stable, body-wide asymmetry once the initial direction is established.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:03:00.640
A bacterial strain isolated from yogurt alters lipid handling pathways in C elegans, according

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.360
to a report from bioengineer.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:06.980
Treated worms maintain mobility and reproductive function longer than controls.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.700
The intervention acts through changes in fat storage gene networks rather than simple

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:12.640
calorie restriction.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:19.660
The same strange shifts fat metabolism gene networks and preserves mobility with age without broad calorie restriction.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:27.260
The result ties a common dietary microbe to targeted changes in aging-related metabolic pathways in a whole organism model.

00:03:28.186 --> 00:03:34.546
University of Florida researchers sent Arabidopsis plants on Blue Origin's new shepherd flight in August 2024,

00:03:35.186 --> 00:03:37.846
with the work published in NPJ microgravity.

00:03:37.846 --> 00:03:42.946
An astronaut carried fixation tubes attached to a flight suit and activated them at four

00:03:42.946 --> 00:03:48.946
mission stages, before launch at microgravity entry at the start of descent and after landing.

00:03:49.546 --> 00:03:53.266
Match control tubes were activated on the ground at identical times.

00:03:53.786 --> 00:03:59.686
More than 1,200 genes showed changed activity, with distinct patterns in leaves versus roots

00:03:59.686 --> 00:04:01.646
and across successive flight phases.

00:04:02.226 --> 00:04:06.866
Many of the responsive genes participate in sensing and reacting to environmental stress.

00:04:06.866 --> 00:04:12.393
older mice retained higher trabecular bone volume when the Sting pathway was inhibited,

00:04:12.813 --> 00:04:18.313
in work from the Lifespan Research Institute, the team measured bone density and microarchitecture

00:04:18.313 --> 00:04:23.653
against untreated age-matched controls. The intervention reduced inflammatory signaling that

00:04:23.653 --> 00:04:29.673
normally accelerates osteoclast activity with age. The work identifies a cellular pathway that can

00:04:29.673 --> 00:04:35.922
be targeted to limit age-related bone loss. North Pacific Spiny Dogfish carry measurable cortisol

00:04:35.922 --> 00:04:39.002
all in their blood, according to a Fizz.org report.

00:04:39.562 --> 00:04:43.902
That steroid helps regulate energy use and stress responses in many vertebrates.

00:04:44.542 --> 00:04:48.402
Earlier assumptions held that sharks rely on different steroids for these functions.

00:04:49.062 --> 00:04:53.422
The new measurements indicate cortisol presence across a broader range of cartilaginous

00:04:53.422 --> 00:04:55.162
fishes than previously recognized.

00:04:56.222 --> 00:05:01.962
Jellyfish relatives and other lineages show repeated amino acid changes at the same sites in a comparative

00:05:01.962 --> 00:05:04.482
genomic analysis covered by Fizz.org.

00:05:04.482 --> 00:05:10.442
These parallel substitutions appear under similar selective pressures, even indistently related groups.

00:05:11.062 --> 00:05:16.042
The pattern suggests convergence at the molecular level is less rare than earlier models predicted.

00:05:16.662 --> 00:05:20.262
The study draws on multiple independent evolutionary transitions.

00:05:21.212 --> 00:05:26.512
Participants predicted strangers' likes and dislikes more accurately when those strangers differed from them,

00:05:26.932 --> 00:05:29.012
